Version: 1.0
desc: Ring Leader Resonator (Mutable Instruments Rings port) by chmaha
tags: resonator modal string physical-modeling instrument effect
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  A resonator in the style of Mutable Instruments Rings: a bank of tuned modes, sympathetic strings,
  a Karplus-Strong string with dispersion and an FM voice, each excited by an internal pluck/strike
  or by whatever audio you feed it.
  Play it from MIDI (each note strums the next voice; chords strum 10 ms apart, as on the module) or
  use it as an effect on a track: in Audio Only mode the input excites the resonator and its
  transients strum it, with the pitch set by the Frequency knob.
  Disastrous Peace is the module's hidden string synth with formant, chorus, reverb and ensemble.
  Pitch bend is +/- 2 semitones.
  Ported from Rings by Emilie Gillet (Mutable Instruments)
  https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack (MIT)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code

slider1:p_freq=0<-30,30,0.01>-Frequency (semitones)
slider2:p_struct=0.5<0,1,0.001>-Structure
slider3:p_bright=0.5<0,1,0.001>-Brightness
slider4:p_damp=0.5<0,1,0.001>-Damping
slider5:p_pos=0.5<0,1,0.001>-Position
slider6:p_model=0<0,5,1{Modal Resonator,Sympathetic Strings,Inharmonic String,FM Voice,Quantized Sympathetic Strings,String and Reverb}>-Model
slider7:p_poly=0<0,2,1{1,2,4}>-Polyphony
slider8:p_input=0<0,2,1{MIDI + Internal Exciter,MIDI + Audio Exciter,Audio Only}>-Input
slider9:p_egg=0<0,1,1{Rings,Disastrous Peace}>-Engine
slider10:p_out=0<-24,12,0.1>-Output (dB)
slider11:p_omode=0<0,1,1{Odd / Even (stereo),Mix (mono)}>-Outputs

in_pin:Left input
in_pin:Right input
out_pin:Odd / Left output
out_pin:Even / Right output
options:no_meter

@init

ext_noinit = gfx_ext_retina = 1;
ext_nodenorm = 1;

function alloc(n) local(r) instance(mp) global() ( r = mp; mp += n; memset(r, 0, n); r; );
alloc.mp = 0;

